OL,3,GNEWSANew food waste plant 'could heat
OL,4,A9,000 homes'
OL,5,
OL,6,FA new #25m facility that could heat
OL,7,Fmore than 9,000 homes by turning food
OL,8,Fwaste into biogas is set to be built.
OL,10,FWiltshire Council has granted
OL,11,Fpermission for the anaerobic digestion
OL,12,Ffacility - where microorganisms will
OL,13,Fbreak down organic matter - at Park
OL,14,FGrounds near the M4 at Royal Wootton
OL,15,FBassett.
OL,17,FEco Sustainable Solutions Ltd, said it
OL,18,Fplans to use the plant to process about
OL,19,F100,000 tonnes of food and liquid waste
OL,20,Fa year, despite concerns from objectors
OL,21,Fabout traffic problems, odour and the
OL,22,Fenvironment.
OL,23,APub: 21-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
